# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv
# The local-selector training environment (torch, transformers, CUDA-less but
# still ~2GB). Deliberately SEPARATE from .venv: training deps must never leak
# into the serving dependency set, which takes only numpy/onnxruntime/tokenizers.
.venv-train/

# Distribution
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Temporary / scratch
.tmp/

# Local skill-learning harness: audit records, proposals, and (when configured to
# a separate overlay dir) generated skill files. The default edit-in-place mode
# writes to the tracked skills dir instead, so those show up in `git diff`.
.daintree/

# Benchmark run outputs (local records, not source)
benchmarks/*/results/

# Testing / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
# Written by the CI coverage step and read by tools/coverage_floors.py.
coverage.json
htmlcov/
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.cache/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# uv (not used by this project; pip + requirements.lock is the source of truth)
uv.lock

# Local skill selection (training side). The SERVING artifacts under
# src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/ are tracked via Git LFS —
# they ship in the image. Everything here is the machinery that produced them and
# is reproducible from `training/`, so it stays out of the repo.
# NOTE: git has no trailing-comment syntax — a "path  # why" line makes the
# comment part of the pattern and silently matches nothing. Keep these bare.
# HuggingFace hub / datasets cache:
training/.cache/
# Trainer checkpoints + tensorboard logs:
training/runs/
# Fine-tuned torch checkpoints, pre-ONNX-export:
training/models/
# Training stdout captures:
training/logs/
# Per-run result JSONs and the report page. Chunky, regenerable, and the numbers
# that matter are transcribed into training/EXPERIMENTS.md — which is the record.
# The report is published as a claude.ai artifact, not carried in the repo.
training/results/
# Generated synthetic corpora are NOT ignored: training/data/*.jsonl is checked in
# as the record of what the shipped weights were trained on.

# Local skill selection (serving side). Model GRAPHS are tracked via Git LFS
# (.gitattributes); these two are not tracked at all:
#   - the skill embedding index, which is rebuilt from the live catalog at Docker
#     build time and on demand in dev, so a committed copy could only ever be
#     stale against a catalog revision it no longer matches;
#   - fp32 graphs, which exist only so the exporter can measure what quantisation
#     costs. Only the served precision ships.
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/**/skill_index.npz
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/index/
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/**/model.onnx
# Legacy retrieve-then-rerank artifacts. That pipeline was measured and
# abandoned (training/EXPERIMENTS.md); the classifier is the shipped selector.
# These are rebuildable from training/export_onnx.py and must not live in the
# repo — three tokenizer vocabularies alone were ~300k lines in any diff view.
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/bi_encoder/
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/reranker/
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/local/artifacts/docs_head.npz
